{"actor":"Galex Yen","comment":null,"created_at":"2026-03-03T21:08:57Z","event_type":"status_changed","id":29,"issue_id":"edgar-diff-vda.11","new_value":"{\"status\":\"in_progress\"}","old_value":"{\"id\":\"edgar-diff-vda.11\",\"title\":\"Spike A: Source mapping prototype\",\"description\":\"Validate that htmlparser2 startIndex/endIndex values provide accurate character-level positions on real SEC HTML. Per architecture doc section 9. Scope: Fetch one real 10-K filing from EDGAR. Build a minimal SAX-based parser using htmlparser2's DomHandler. Identify 5 section boundaries. Verify html.slice(node.startIndex, node.endIndex) captures expected content. Test with multi-byte characters. Deliverable: spikes/source-mapping/ with runnable TypeScript and NOTES.md documenting character-vs-byte behavior, CDATA/comment anomalies, parse time, API stability. Success criteria: All 5 offset checks pass, multi-byte behavior documented, parse time \\u003c 500ms. Fallback: two-pass with linkedom + string scanning. Time box: 2 days.\",\"status\":\"open\",\"priority\":1,\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"owner\":\"galexy@users.noreply.github.com\",\"created_at\":\"2026-02-27T00:35:59Z\",\"created_by\":\"Galex Yen\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-02-27T00:35:59Z\"}"}
